  "reference_text": "For teenagers aged 13–17, CDC lists 8–10 hours of sleep daily as a general recommendation. Sleep quality also matters. Sleep difficulties or symptoms of a sleep disorder should be discussed with a healthcare provider. This reference is not an individualized basketball prescription or an adopted planning threshold.",
